IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- =====================================================================
-- CASE STUDY: REGULATION — PDPA DBNO
-- Personal Data Protection Act · Data Breach Notification Obligation
--
-- This is a technology prototype, not legal advice.
--
-- Modern-L4 transcription of the legacy "LegalSS" spreadsheet encoding
-- of a fragment of Singapore's Personal Data Protection Act, Part VIA,
-- read together with the PDP (Notification of Data Breaches) Regulations
-- and the PDPC Advisory Guidelines, Part 20.
--
-- Generally, if an organisation experiences a data breach, it has 30 days
-- to assess it. If the breach turns out to be Notifiable, the organisation
-- has 3 days to inform both the PDPC and the affected individuals.
-- =====================================================================

§ `Singapore Personal Data Protection Act — Data Breach Notification`
@ref-src Act Part VIA; PDP (Notification of Data Breaches) Regulations; Advisory Guidelines Part 20


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Ontology`
-- =====================================================================

-- Act §26 First Schedule, Part 1 — the prescribed personal data whose
-- breach is taken to result in significant harm to the individual.
DECLARE `Schedule Part 1 Category` IS ONE OF
    `1 remuneration`
    `2 income from sale of goods or property`
    `3 credit, charge or debit card number`
    `4 account number with a bank or finance company`
    `5 identification as a child or young person under the CYPA`
    `6 identification of a vulnerable adult under the VAA`
    `7 private key for a secure electronic record or signature`
    `8 net worth`
    `9 deposit of moneys with an organisation`
    `10 withdrawal of deposited moneys`
    `11 advances, loans and other credit facilities`
    `12 liabilities incurred on the individual's behalf`
    `13 payment of moneys or transfer of property to the individual`
    `14 creditworthiness`
    `15 investment in capital markets products`
    `16 existence and amount of any debt`
    `17 insurance policy terms, premiums, benefits and claims`
    `18 health assessment, diagnosis, treatment or prevention`
    `19 treatment relating to human reproduction`
    `20 organ donation, removal or transplantation`
    `21 suicide or attempted suicide`
    `22 domestic, child or sexual abuse`
    `23 adoption matters`

-- The closed-world set of facts that describe one data-breach scenario.
-- Each "GIVEN" line in the legacy scenario tests sets one of these fields.
DECLARE `Data Breach` HAS
    -- Act §26A(2)(a): an unauthorised act in relation to personal data
    `unauthorised access`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `unauthorised use`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `unauthorised copying`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `unauthorised modification`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Act §26A(2)(b): loss of a storage medium where such an act is likely
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Act §26B(4): exception where the breach is confined within one organisation
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Regs 3(1)(a): personal identifiers
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Act §26B(2)(a) read with Part 1 (subject to Part 2) of the Schedule
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS A LIST OF `Schedule Part 1 Category`
    -- Act §26B(3): scale
    `number of affected individuals` IS A NUMBER
    -- Act §26D(5): remediation exceptions to notifying individuals
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Act §26D(6)(a): PDPC waiver / exclusion of individual notification
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Act §4(1)(c): public-agency carve-out
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS A BOOLEAN


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Constitutive rules — NDB Qualification`
-- =====================================================================

-- Act §26A: "a data breach occurred"
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `an unauthorised act in relation to personal data occurred` IF
       breach's `unauthorised access`
    OR breach's `unauthorised use`
    OR breach's `unauthorised disclosure`
    OR breach's `unauthorised copying`
    OR breach's `unauthorised modification`
    OR breach's `unauthorised disposal`

GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `a data breach occurred` IF
       `an unauthorised act in relation to personal data occurred` breach
    OR breach's `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely`

-- Regs 3(1)(a): the breach relates to a prescribed personal identifier
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `the breach relates to a prescribed personal identifier` IF
       breach's `relates to the individual's full name`
    OR breach's `relates to the individual's alias`
    OR breach's `relates to the individual's identification number`

-- Act §26B(2)(a) read with Part 1 of the Schedule: at least one prescribed
-- category of personal data is involved.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `the breach relates to a prescribed Part 1 category` IF
    CONSIDER breach's `prescribed personal data involved`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE       TRUE

-- Act §26B(1)(a) and (2): the breach results in, or is likely to result in,
-- significant harm to an affected individual.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `the breach is likely to result in significant harm` IF
        `the breach relates to a prescribed personal identifier` breach
    AND `the breach relates to a prescribed Part 1 category` breach

-- Act §26B(3): the prescribed threshold of affected individuals.
`the prescribed threshold of affected individuals` MEANS 500

-- Act §26B(1)(b) and (3): the breach is, or is likely to be, of a
-- significant scale.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
DECIDE `the breach is of significant scale` IF
    breach's `number of affected individuals`
        GREATER THAN `the prescribed threshold of affected individuals`

-- Act §26B: it is a Notifiable Data Breach.
@export Decide whether a data breach is a Notifiable Data Breach under Part VIA of the Singapore PDPA.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach` @desc The facts of the data breach being assessed.
DECIDE `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` IF
        `a data breach occurred` breach
    AND NOT breach's `occurred only within an organisation`
    AND (   `the breach is likely to result in significant harm` breach
         OR `the breach is of significant scale` breach )


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Constitutive rules — derived obligations`
-- =====================================================================

-- Act §26D(1) read with §4(1)(c): the organisation must notify the PDPC.
@export Decide whether the organisation is obliged to notify the PDPC of the breach.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach` @desc The facts of the data breach being assessed.
DECIDE `the organisation must notify the PDPC` IF
        `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` breach
    AND NOT breach's `the organisation is a public agency`

-- Act §26D(2) read with §26D(5)–(6) and §4(1)(c): the organisation must
-- notify the affected individuals, unless a remediation or exclusion applies.
@export Decide whether the organisation is obliged to notify the affected individuals of the breach.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach` @desc The facts of the data breach being assessed.
DECIDE `the organisation must notify the affected individuals` IF
        `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` breach
    AND NOT breach's `the organisation is a public agency`
    AND NOT breach's `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`
    AND NOT breach's `organisation had implemented a technological measure`
    AND NOT breach's `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals`


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Regulative rules — parties and actions`
-- =====================================================================

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the Organisation`
    `the PDPC`

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `assess whether the breach is notifiable`
    `notify the PDPC`
    `notify the affected individuals`
    `query for an explanation of inaction`
    `respond to the PDPC with an explanation of the inaction`


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Regulative rules — PHASE 1: ASSESS`
-- =====================================================================

-- Act §26C(2): every organisation that is not a public agency, upon becoming
-- aware that a data breach may have occurred, must assess within 30 days
-- whether it is a Notifiable Data Breach.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
`Assessment` breach MEANS
    PARTY  `the Organisation`
    MUST   `assess whether the breach is notifiable`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  `Notification` breach
    LEST   `PDPC query with demand`

-- The PDPC may query the organisation, demanding an explanation of inaction.
`PDPC query with demand` MEANS
    PARTY `the PDPC`
    MAY   `query for an explanation of inaction`
    HENCE `Respond to PDPC`

-- Having been queried, the organisation must respond to the PDPC.
`Respond to PDPC` MEANS
    PARTY `the Organisation`
    MUST  `respond to the PDPC with an explanation of the inaction`


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Regulative rules — PHASE 2: NOTIFY`
-- =====================================================================

-- Act §26D: Notification = notify the PDPC AND notify the individuals.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
`Notification` breach MEANS
    `Notify PDPC` breach
    RAND
    `Notify Individuals` breach

-- Act §26D(1): within 3 days, if it is a Notifiable Data Breach (and you
-- are not a public agency), notify the PDPC.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
`Notify PDPC` breach MEANS
    IF   `the organisation must notify the PDPC` breach
    THEN PARTY  `the Organisation`
         MUST   `notify the PDPC`
         WITHIN 3
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the Organisation`
                BECAUSE "failed to notify the PDPC within 3 days of assessing the breach as notifiable"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Act §26D(2): within 3 days, notify each of the affected individuals,
-- unless a §26D(5) remediation or a §26D(6) exclusion applies.
GIVEN breach IS A `Data Breach`
`Notify Individuals` breach MEANS
    IF   `the organisation must notify the affected individuals` breach
    THEN PARTY  `the Organisation`
         MUST   `notify the affected individuals`
         WITHIN 3
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the Organisation`
                BECAUSE "failed to notify the affected individuals within 3 days"
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Scenario testing`
-- =====================================================================

-- L4 records have no functional-update syntax, so each scenario is built in
-- full. Reading a column of values top-to-bottom recovers the "GIVEN" lists of
-- the legacy spreadsheet scenarios.

-- Advisory Guidelines p130 — Misplaced storage drive.
-- Loss of storage medium with likely disposal, but the breach occurred only
-- within the organisation. EXPECT: NOT a Notifiable Data Breach.
`Misplaced storage drive` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS FALSE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS FALSE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS TRUE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS FALSE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `13 payment of moneys or transfer of property to the individual`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 0
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `Misplaced storage drive`)

-- Advisory Guidelines p131 (20.2) — ABC. Unauthorised disclosure; relates to
-- full name and credit-card number. EXPECT: NDB; notify PDPC and individuals.
`ABC` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS FALSE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS TRUE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS FALSE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `3 credit, charge or debit card number`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 200
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `ABC`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the PDPC` `ABC`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the affected individuals` `ABC`

-- Advisory Guidelines p131 (20.2) — DEF and GHI. As ABC, but the PDPC, in
-- consultation, agrees ABC is best placed to notify, so DEF/GHI are
-- prohibited from notifying the individuals.
-- EXPECT: NDB; notify PDPC; do NOT notify individuals.
`DEF and GHI` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS FALSE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS TRUE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS FALSE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `3 credit, charge or debit card number`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 200
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS TRUE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `DEF and GHI`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the PDPC` `DEF and GHI`
#ASSERT NOT (`the organisation must notify the affected individuals` `DEF and GHI`)

-- Advisory Guidelines p138 (20.3) — Unauthorised access of patients' medical
-- records. 50 affected (below the scale threshold), but significant harm via
-- identification number + a health-diagnosis category.
-- EXPECT: NDB; notify PDPC and individuals.
`Patient records` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS TRUE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS FALSE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS TRUE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `18 health assessment, diagnosis, treatment or prevention`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 50
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `Patient records`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the PDPC` `Patient records`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the affected individuals` `Patient records`

-- Advisory Guidelines p139 (20.4) — Theft of portable storage drive with hotel
-- guests' details. 1000 affected (significant scale) and significant harm.
-- EXPECT: NDB; notify PDPC and individuals.
`Hotel drive` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS TRUE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS FALSE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS TRUE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `3 credit, charge or debit card number`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 1000
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `Hotel drive`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the affected individuals` `Hotel drive`

-- Advisory Guidelines p141 (20.7) — Disclosure of 250 students' library loan
-- history. 250 affected, no significant harm. EXPECT: not significant scale;
-- NOT a Notifiable Data Breach.
`Library loans` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS FALSE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS TRUE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS FALSE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS EMPTY
    `number of affected individuals` IS 250
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS FALSE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`the breach is of significant scale` `Library loans`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `Library loans`)

-- Advisory Guidelines p142 (20.9) — Disclosure of an email attachment with the
-- personal data of 1000 customers. Significant scale and significant harm, but
-- the organisation has taken action rendering harm unlikely (§26D(5)).
-- EXPECT: NDB; notify PDPC; do NOT notify individuals.
`Remediated email` MEANS `Data Breach` WITH
    `unauthorised access`        IS FALSE
    `unauthorised use`           IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disclosure`    IS TRUE
    `unauthorised copying`       IS FALSE
    `unauthorised modification`  IS FALSE
    `unauthorised disposal`      IS FALSE
    `loss of storage medium making an unauthorised act likely` IS FALSE
    `occurred only within an organisation` IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's full name`             IS TRUE
    `relates to the individual's alias`                 IS FALSE
    `relates to the individual's identification number` IS FALSE
    `prescribed personal data involved` IS LIST `3 credit, charge or debit card number`
    `number of affected individuals` IS 1000
    `organisation took action rendering harm unlikely`     IS TRUE
    `organisation had implemented a technological measure`  IS FALSE
    `PDPC has prohibited notification of individuals` IS FALSE
    `the organisation is a public agency` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `Remediated email`
#ASSERT `the organisation must notify the PDPC` `Remediated email`
#ASSERT NOT (`the organisation must notify the affected individuals` `Remediated email`)


-- =====================================================================
§§ `Regulative trace — the happy path`
-- =====================================================================

-- Drive the Assessment obligation for the ABC scenario: the organisation
-- assesses in time, then notifies both the PDPC and the individuals in time.
#EVAL `it is a Notifiable Data Breach` `ABC`

#TRACE `Assessment` `ABC` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Organisation` DOES `assess whether the breach is notifiable` AT 20
    PARTY `the Organisation` DOES `notify the PDPC`                         AT 22
    PARTY `the Organisation` DOES `notify the affected individuals`         AT 22
